[groq-gpt-oss] evals/prompts/lib/skill-p:
Below is a quick-reference guide that shows **all the practical ways you can add a search / geocoder box to a Mapbox GL JS v2 map**.  
It’s split into three sections:

| Section | What you get | When you’d use it | Key trade-offs |
|---------|--------------|-------------------|----------------|
| **A. Mapbox-official** | `mapbox-gl-geocoder` (or the newer **Mapbox Search UI**) | You already have a Mapbox access token and are happy to pay for Mapbox Geocoding (or stay within the free tier). | Proprietary, token-required, rate-limited by Mapbox, but the UI is polished and tightly integrated. |
| **B. Open-source UI + open geocoder** | `maplibre-gl-geocoder` (or other UI libs) + any public/open geocoding service (Nominatim, Photon, Pelias, OpenCage, MapTiler, etc.) | You want to avoid Mapbox fees, keep the UI open-source, or you already run a self-hosted geocoder. | You must handle attribution, CORS, and possibly host the UI yourself; some services have stricter usage policies. |
| **C. DIY UI + any API** | Build your own `<input>` + fetch → any HTTP geocoder (including commercial ones like HERE, TomTom, Google) | You need a custom look-and-feel, want to combine multiple providers, or need extra fields (e.g., POI type filters). | More code to maintain; you lose the “plug-and-play” conveniences of the ready-made widgets. |

Below you’ll find **step-by-step code snippets** for each option, plus a short checklist of things to watch (tokens, CORS, attribution, rate limits, licensing).  

---

## A. Mapbox-official geocoder

### 1️⃣ `mapbox-gl-geocoder` (the classic widget)

| Feature | Details |
|---------|---------|
| **Package** | `@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder` |
| **Requires** | A valid Mapbox access token (`mapboxgl.accessToken`) |
| **Works with** | Mapbox GL JS v2 (and v1) – no changes needed |
| **UI** | Search box + dropdown, optional “proximity” bias, language support |
| **Pricing** | Uses Mapbox Geocoding API → counts against your Mapbox usage (free tier: 100 k requests / month). |
| **License** | BSD-3 (open source) but the underlying geocoding service is proprietary. |

#### Installation

```bash
npm i mapbox-gl @mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder
# or via CDN
# <script src="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/v2.15.0/mapbox-gl.js"></script>
# <script src="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/plugins/mapbox-gl-geocoder/v4.7.2/mapbox-gl-geocoder.min.js"></script>
```

#### Basic usage

```javascript
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
import MapboxGeocoder from '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder';
import '@mapbox/mapbox-gl-geocoder/dist/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css';

mapboxgl.accessToken = 'YOUR_MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN';

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});

// Add the geocoder control
const geocoder = new MapboxGeocoder({
  accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken,
  mapboxgl: mapboxgl,          // required for the built-in marker
  placeholder: 'Search places…',
  proximity: { longitude: -122.42, latitude: 37.78 }, // optional bias
  language: 'en',
  countries: 'us',             // optional filter
  limit: 5                     // max results per query
});

map.addControl(geocoder, 'top-left');
```

**Optional tweaks**

| What | How |
|------|-----|
| **Hide the default marker** | `geocoder.setRenderFunction((result) => { /* custom HTML */ })` or `geocoder.on('result', e => e.result.geometry && map.getSource('geocoder-result').setData(e.result.geometry))` |
| **Bias to map viewport** | `geocoder.setProximity(map.getCenter())` on `moveend` |
| **Custom CSS** | Override `.mapboxgl-ctrl-geocoder` in your stylesheet. |
| **Internationalization** | Pass `language: ['en', 'es']` or `localGeocoder` for your own service. |

### 2️⃣ **Mapbox Search UI** (newer, more feature-rich)

- **Package**: `@mapbox/search-js` (beta as of 2024-09).  
- **Why use it?** It adds “search as you type” with fuzzy matching, category filters, and a modern UI that matches Mapbox’s own web apps.  
- **How to add** (quick example):

```bash
npm i @mapbox/search-js mapbox-gl
```

```javascript
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';
import { SearchBox } from '@mapbox/search-js';
import '@mapbox/search-js/dist/search.css';

mapboxgl.accessToken = 'YOUR_TOKEN';
const map = new mapboxgl.Map({ /* … */ });

const searchBox = new SearchBox({
  accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken,
  container: 'search-container', // any div you create
  placeholder: 'Search…',
  // optional: limit, language, countries, etc.
});

searchBox.on('result', (e) => {
  const { center } = e.result.geometry;
  map.flyTo({ center, zoom: 14 });
});
```

> **Note:** The Search UI still uses the Mapbox Geocoding API under the hood, so the same token & usage limits apply.

---

## B. Open-source UI + open geocoder

If you want to **avoid Mapbox fees or tokens**, you can keep the same UI component (`maplibre-gl-geocoder`) and point it at a free/open geocoding service. The UI works **unchanged** with Mapbox GL JS v2 because it only depends on the `mapboxgl` object for map interaction.

| Service | Endpoint (public demo) | Attribution requirement | Typical free-tier limits |
|---------|------------------------|------------------------|--------------------------|
| **Nominatim (OpenStreetMap)** | `https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search?format=geojson&q={query}` | “© OpenStreetMap contributors” | 1 req/s per IP (public instance) – not for production. |
| **Photon (Komoot)** | `https://photon.komoot.io/api/?q={query}` | “© OpenStreetMap contributors” | No hard rate-limit, but heavy usage discouraged. |
| **Pelias (Geocode.earth)** | `https://api.geocode.earth/v1/autocomplete?text={query}` | “© OpenStreetMap contributors” | Free tier: 2 k req/day. |
| **OpenCage** | `https://api.opencagedata.com/geocode/v1/json?q={query}&key=YOUR_KEY` | “© OpenStreetMap contributors” | 2 500 req/day free. |
| **MapTiler Geocoding** | `https://api.maptiler.com/geocoding/{query}.json?key=YOUR_KEY` | “© OpenStreetMap contributors” | 100 k req/month free. |
| **Self-hosted Nominatim / Photon / Pelias** | Your own URL | Same OSM attribution | Unlimited (subject to your own hardware). |

### 1️⃣ `maplibre-gl-geocoder` (UI component)

| Install | Code |
|---------|------|
| **npm** | `npm i maplibre-gl @maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder` |
| **CDN** | `<script src="https://unpkg.com/@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder@latest/dist/maplibre-gl-geocoder.min.js"></script>` |

> **Important:** The package name is `@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder`. It works with **both** MapLibre GL JS **and** Mapbox GL JS (v1/v2) because it only expects a `mapboxgl`-compatible object.

#### Example: Nominatim (public demo)

```javascript
import mapboxgl from 'mapbox-gl';               // you already have v2 loaded
import { MapLibreGeocoder } from '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder';
import '@maplibre/maplibre-gl-geocoder/dist/maplibre-gl-geocoder.css';

// No token needed for Nominatim
const geocoder = new MapLibreGeocoder({
  // `mapboxgl` is required for the built-in marker handling
  mapboxgl: mapboxgl,
  // custom forwardGeocoder that talks to Nominatim
  forwardGeocoder: (query) => {
    const url = new URL('https://nominatim.openstreetmap.org/search');
    url.search = new URLSearchParams({
      q: query,
      format: 'geojson',
      addressdetails: 1,
      limit: 5,
    });
    return fetch(url)
      .then(res => res.json())
      .then(data => {
        // Nominatim returns GeoJSON FeatureCollection – adapt to the format
        return {
          type: 'FeatureCollection',
          features: data.features.map(f => ({
            ...f,
            place_name: f.properties.display_name,
            center: f.geometry.coordinates,
            // MapLibreGeocoder expects `place_name` and `center`
          }))
        };
      });
  },
  placeholder: 'Search OSM…',
  // optional: you can also set `reverseGeocoder` if you need reverse lookup
});

map.addControl(geocoder, 'top-left');
```

#### Example: MapTiler Geocoding (requires API key)

```javascript
const geocoder = new MapLibreGeocoder({
  mapboxgl,
  forwardGeocoder: (query) => {
    const url = `https://api.maptiler.com/geocoding/${encodeURIComponent(query)}.json?key=YOUR_MAPTILER_KEY&limit=5`;
    return fetch(url)
      .then(r => r.json())
      .then(data => ({
        type: 'FeatureCollection',
        features: data.features.map(f => ({
          ...f,
          place_name: f.properties.formatted,
          center: f.geometry.coordinates
        }))
      }));
  },
  placeholder: 'Search MapTiler…',
});
```

#### Styling & CSS

All the default class names are **`maplibregl-ctrl-geocoder`** (instead of `mapboxgl-`). If you already have CSS that targets the Mapbox class, just duplicate/rename it.

```css
.maplibregl-ctrl-geocoder {
  /* your custom styles */
}
```

### 2️⃣ Other UI libraries (if you don’t like the default widget)

| Library | Compatibility | Quick note |
|---------|---------------|------------|
| **Leaflet Control Geocoder** (ported) | Works with any map that can accept a DOM element; you can embed it next to a Mapbox GL container. | Good if you already use Leaflet elsewhere. |
| **Algolia Places** (deprecated) | Still works but Algolia is shutting it down; not recommended. |
| **React-Map-GL / React-MapLibre-GL** | Use `<Geocoder>` component from `react-map-gl-geocoder` (works with Mapbox GL) or `react-map-gl-geocoder` fork for MapLibre. | Ideal for React projects. |
| **Vue-Mapbox / Vue-MapLibre** | `vue-mapbox-geocoder` component (forked from Mapbox). | Ideal for Vue. |

All of these simply need a **forwardGeocoder** function that returns a GeoJSON `FeatureCollection` in the shape shown above.

---

